\last_approved\\acts.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":750,"oldLines":3,"newStart":750,"newLines":9,"lines":[" date = \"2026-10-16\""," approved = []"," reattested = [\"LLR-313\", \"TC-333\"]","+","+[[act]]","+seq = 124","+date = \"2026-10-17\"","+approved = []","+reattested = [\"LLR-300\", \"TC-339\"]"]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-928\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\requirements\\low-level-requirements.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":3173,"oldLines":8,"newStart":3173,"newLines":8,"lines":[" sr_refs = [\"SR-229\", \"SR-237\"]"," title = \"Coordinator context occupancy, lease, and drain latch\""," module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/coordinator_guard.py;project-trajectory/scripts/integrate.py;project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/shell_line.py\"","-code_symbol = \"GuardConfig/guard_config/Occupancy/read_occupancy/lease_dir/take/release/clear/hand_back/record_event/latch_reading/window_refusal/claim_refusal/on_blackout/launch_reason/model_clis/command_name/command_words/_assigned/_invoked/window_check/hooks_state/enable_hooks/on_monitored/on_session_start/on_pre_compact/classify_compaction/hook;claim;segments/Unreadable/Word\"","-detail = \"guard_config reads the declared coordinator threshold and window: a non-positive, out-of-range or malformed threshold is off and a malformed window reads as the default. read_occupancy reads the newest valid assistant usage after the live transcript branch's latest compaction boundary, never a sidechain record, counting input and cached input; a record whose usage is malformed, partial or zero is skipped, and no valid usage reads as unknown, never zero. A primary-checkout lease names one coordinator session and its transcript. take refuses another holder; release frees the lease and clear unlatches it, each requiring and recording the owner's reason; hand_back accepts only the holder session and a handoff carrying a session prompt, frees the lease, and records the handoff; it refuses another or unnamed caller, whatever handoff it names, while naming the owner's release; it refuses the holder's own pending relaunch request, while a previous holder's request does not block it and is left for session_end's foreign-request refusal; with the guard off it returns before reading or writing. Elapsed time never transfers ownership. on_session_start installs a session as holder, unlatched, only when it presents the successor token the holder's exit wrote into the lease, and restates a latched drain to the holder's own resumed start. Only the holder's own hook payload on the holder's transcript is measured, never a subagent's. latch_reading latches drain when the unrounded reading reaches the threshold and retains it through lower readings, compaction and resume; it ends only through the owner's clear, the owner's release, the holder's hand-back, or a successor take. window_refusal runs before the dial on every claim route, including the dispatcher, naming the UTC end; the dispatcher remains exempt only from the context guard. claim_refusal identifies the claimant by the session id the agent CLI exports to its tool processes (CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID), refuses with no lease held or a claimant that is not the holder, and reads and latches the holder's transcript itself, so a refusal never depends on a hook having run; a claim holding the dispatch lock never calls it. While a window is armed hooks act at every dial and deny the closed list of the main session's Agent call, SendMessage call, Bash/PowerShell model-CLI command word, and a Bash/PowerShell line unreadable only because of an unclosed single quote, unclosed double quote, unclosed POSIX dollar quote, unclosed POSIX backtick substitution, unclosed dollar-parenthesis substitution, or unclosed PowerShell here-string. One quote-aware shell reading per dialect reads quoted assignments and env split strings as the shell does, reads a PowerShell assignment, recognised by an unquoted assignment operator wherever it stands (quotedness is known for every character of a word), whatever its target, as running its right-hand command; a quoted right-hand value and a variable right-hand value stay data, while a chained assignment whose final right-hand side is a command runs that command; treats quoted separators as data, reads substitutions in unquoted here-document and double-quoted PowerShell here-string bodies, and keeps quoted bodies as data; window_check exits nonzero inside it. At every SessionStart inside a window, hooks inject the blackout close-down instruction; each main session's monitored events inject it at that session's first monitored event in the window and every twentieth thereafter, counted per session per window: bring each open lane to its pause point, using a wrap-up adjudication for an active claim where needed; write the handoff naming each lane and its next obligation; request no relaunch; and end the session. Hook responses inject the latch instruction once and bounded reminders thereafter; inside a blackout window the latch is still recorded, but the blackout close-down, which requests no relaunch, is injected in its place. PreCompact records trigger, occupancy and latch/request state; classify_compaction reports missed-threshold, manual and during-drain cases.\"","+code_symbol = \"GuardConfig/guard_config/Occupancy/read_occupancy/lease_dir/take/release/clear/hand_back/record_event/latch_reading/window_refusal/claim_refusal/on_blackout/launch_reason/model_clis/command_name/command_words/_assigned/window_check/hooks_state/enable_hooks/on_monitored/on_session_start/on_pre_compact/classify_compaction/hook;claim;segments/Unreadable/Word\"","+detail = \"guard_config reads the declared coordinator threshold and window: a non-positive, out-of-range or malformed threshold is off and a malformed window reads as the default. read_occupancy reads the newest valid assistant usage after the live transcript branch's latest compaction boundary, never a sidechain record, counting input and cached input; a record whose usage is malformed, partial or zero is skipped, and no valid usage reads as unknown, never zero. A primary-checkout lease names one coordinator session and its transcript. take refuses another holder; release frees the lease and clear unlatches it, each requiring and recording the owner's reason; hand_back accepts only the holder session and a handoff carrying a session prompt, frees the lease, and records the handoff; it refuses another or unnamed caller, whatever handoff it names, while naming the owner's release; it refuses the holder's own pending relaunch request, while a previous holder's request does not block it and is left for session_end's foreign-request refusal; with the guard off it returns before reading or writing. Elapsed time never transfers ownership. on_session_start installs a session as holder, unlatched, only when it presents the successor token the holder's exit wrote into the lease, and restates a latched drain to the holder's own resumed start. Only the holder's own hook payload on the holder's transcript is measured, never a subagent's. latch_reading latches drain when the unrounded reading reaches the threshold and retains it through lower readings, compaction and resume; it ends only through the owner's clear, the owner's release, the holder's hand-back, or a successor take. window_refusal runs before the dial on every claim route, including the dispatcher, naming the UTC end; the dispatcher remains exempt only from the context guard. claim_refusal identifies the claimant by the session id the agent CLI exports to its tool processes (CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID), refuses with no lease held or a claimant that is not the holder, and reads and latches the holder's transcript itself, so a refusal never depends on a hook having run; a claim holding the dispatch lock never calls it. While a window is armed hooks act at every dial and deny the closed list of the main session's Agent call, SendMessage call, Bash/PowerShell model-CLI command word, and a Bash/PowerShell line unreadable only because of an unclosed single quote, unclosed double quote, unclosed POSIX dollar quote, unclosed POSIX backtick substitution, unclosed dollar-parenthesis substitution, or unclosed PowerShell here-string. One quote-aware shell reading per dialect reads quoted values as the shell does, and treats quoted separators, comments and here-document and here-string bodies as data. It finds the model-CLI command word after leading variable assignments, the timeout and env prefixes, the shell's reserved words, the chain operators and the call operator, and in substitutions written in the line or inside double quotes. It reads a PowerShell assignment to a variable as running its right-hand command, while a quoted or variable right-hand value stays data. A form outside this list gets no dedicated recognition: it may incidentally match this reading, and carries no guarantee either way. window_check exits nonzero inside an armed window. At every SessionStart inside a window, hooks inject the blackout close-down instruction; each main session's monitored events inject it at that session's first monitored event in the window and every twentieth thereafter, counted per session per window: bring each open lane to its pause point, using a wrap-up adjudication for an active claim where needed; write the handoff naming each lane and its next obligation; request no relaunch; and end the session. Hook responses inject the latch instruction once and bounded reminders thereafter; inside a blackout window the latch is still recorded, but the blackout close-down, which requests no relaunch, is injected in its place. PreCompact records trigger, occupancy and latch/request state; classify_compaction reports missed-threshold, manual and during-drain cases.\""," rationale = \"The context reading and lease are one admission fact: without one holder and a latched record, a tool-event observation can be missed and a later claim can start new work after the coordinator should be closing out.\""," test_refs = \"TC-315;TC-316;TC-317\""," status = \"Approved\""]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-928\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\test\\test-cases.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":3444,"oldLines":9,"newStart":3444,"newLines":9,"lines":[" [test.TC-339]"," verifies = [\"SR-229\", \"LLR-300\", \"IF-271\", \"IF-274\", \"IF-275\", \"SR-237\"]"," level = \"Integration\"","-method = \"Exercise claims and hooks during blackout with the context guard off. Exercise quote-aware shell reading, PowerShell assignments of any target form (property, index, array-type, scoped, comma list, chained), with the operator spaced or written against a word that holds a quoted piece, and with command, quoted and variable right-hand sides, expandable and literal here bodies, and unreadable-line denial. Assert every SessionStart inside a window provides the close-down instruction and, for each main session, its first monitored event in that window and every twentieth thereafter provide it; assert that the route registry supplies model-CLI names.\"","+method = \"Exercise claims and hooks during blackout with the context guard off. Exercise quote-aware shell reading, PowerShell assignments to a variable (plain, typed, scoped, comma list, compound operator) with command, quoted and variable right-hand sides, here-document and here-string bodies, and unreadable-line denial. Assert every SessionStart inside a window provides the close-down instruction and, for each main session, its first monitored event in that window and every twentieth thereafter provide it; assert that the route registry supplies model-CLI names.\""," tier = \"Smoke\"","-expected = \"Claims refuse on both routes and hooks deny only declared main-session launch forms. Quote-aware words, PowerShell assignments whose right-hand side runs a model, and expandable bodies that launch a model are denied; quoted bodies and quoted or variable right-hand values are allowed; unreadable shell input is denied. The close-down instruction appears at every SessionStart inside a window and, for each main session, at its first monitored event in that window and every twentieth thereafter; it names each lane's handoff obligation, instructs no relaunch before the session ends, and model-CLI names follow the route registry.\"","+expected = \"Claims refuse on both routes and hooks deny only declared main-session launch forms. Quote-aware words, PowerShell assignments to a variable whose right-hand side runs a model are denied; here-document and here-string bodies and quoted or variable right-hand values are allowed; unreadable shell input is denied. The close-down instruction appears at every SessionStart inside a window and, for each main session, at its first monitored event in that window and every twentieth thereafter; it names each lane's handoff obligation, instructs no relaunch before the session ends, and model-CLI names follow the route registry.\""," automated = \"Yes\""," evidence = \"tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_a_claim_inside_the_window_is_refused_with_the_guard_off; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_the_dispatchers_claim_is_refused_inside_the_window; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_the_hooks_deny_each_launch_form_with_the_guard_off; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_the_hooks_allow_everything_else; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_a_subagents_call_is_never_denied; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_a_quoted_launch_form_is_denied; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_a_quoted_operator_is_not_a_command_boundary; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_an_unreadable_command_line_is_denied_inside_the_window; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_the_one_reading_keeps_quoted_text_in_its_word; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_a_json_array_template_names_its_cli; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_session_start_and_the_monitored_events_tell_the_close_down; tests/test_blackout_window.py::test_the_cli_names_come_from_the_route_registry\""," status = \"Approved\""]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-928\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\README.md","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-928\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\acts.toml","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-928\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\requirements\\low-level-requirements.toml","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-928\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\test\\test-cases.toml"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Wtgim7DR1fqtEcpajn65Zs","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
