{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg7JNF14CKpCkCVkiQMhH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both rows changed meaning, and I blessed and re-anchored both. Two commits, each ending `WI: WI-928`, and the commit checks passed on both:\n\n| Commit | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| `ac7bbac6e` | The verdict under `## amendment`: `VERDICT: MEANING rows=2`, then `SITTING: JUDGED kinds=amendment`. The kit's parser accepts it under the combined binding. |\n| `62eb15881` | `snapshot --reattests LLR-300,TC-339`. No other drifted row blocked the copy. |\n\n**Why meaning:** the blackout hook now denies fewer shell forms.\n- **No longer denied:** a model call inside an expandable here-document or here-string body, and a PowerShell assignment to a property, index or typed-array target. Both were denied before and now carry no guarantee.\n- **Still denied:**\n  - the quote-aware reading;\n  - the command word after assignments, `timeout`/`env` prefixes, reserved words, chain operators and the call operator, or inside a substitution;\n  - assignment to a variable, such as `$r = claude -p x`;\n  - unreadable lines, and Agent and SendMessage calls.\n\nLLR-300 now also says plainly that any form outside its list gets no dedicated recognition. TC-339 drops exactly the tests for the removed forms and keeps the rest, and all of its cited tests exist.\n\n**Why blessed:**\n- **The owner ruled these forms contrived** (D-011). They came from single review rounds and two dispute sittings, under an open-ended promise to catch \"a model CLI as any command word\".\n- **No kit route reopens.** Every kit-owned launch point already refuses inside an armed window by construction: session-service admission, claim routes, keep-warm and `window-check`. The hook only guards a CLI an agent types straight into its shell, and WI-834 ruled that stop encouraged, not enforced.\n- **The new bound is better text.** A closed list plus an explicit \"no guarantee beyond it\" replaces the open-world promise that caused the churn.\n\n**One thing to be aware of:** this removes deny cases, so a model call hidden in an expandable here body, which the old guard caught, now runs during a blackout. I'm comfortable blessing that because the owner ruled it out and the kit's own launch points still refuse. If it should be closed properly, the by-construction alternative of refusing at the launch point is recorded as deliberately not built (D-016).\n\nThe untracked `003-ADJUDICATE-bcb892f.md.requested` is the coordinator's, and I didn't touch it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":820,"cache_read_input_tokens":673021,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":820},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"73ae5cf9-d335-4bb7-a08f-7631da597f26","uuid":"cae0b5c9-d96a-44fa-9872-b6e49bc0b1b6","timestamp":"2026-10-17T06:01:22.290Z","request_id":"req_011Cg7JNDPZStL9HtF5Duk13"}
